# The staging-box template — a thin, creds-free, server-class seed (#81, the
# re-cut of #69's layering): Debian 13, the 'ops' user and tmux. The server
# posture — docker, sshd hardening — is OPERATOR-run, converged inside the box
# after box has minted it (#214), exactly as the tailnet workload join beside
# it always was: that one holds a pre-auth key box must never see, and this
# one was only ever auto-run because box used to install a converger into its
# guests. It no longer does. The template keeps its name, suffix and all: it
# is the name a fleet's records, its runbooks and its converger's own role
# registry already use, and renaming it would move a string nothing else
# moved. Server-CLASS, not a fleet machine — this is still a box tenant.
# KEY="value" only. Parsed against an allowlist, never sourced; there is no
# key for a network or a security flag, on purpose — the shared box-profile
# profile is the placement contract and no template can weaken it.
# The two boot demands (#68): the VM is this box's trust boundary and its
# guest runs docker, so no container fallback (BOX_REQUIRE_VM); and a server
# must return from a host reboot without an operator (BOX_AUTOSTART).
# BOX_USER must match the user user-data.yaml creates (the duplication is
# deliberate and by hand) — and it is the user the operator's convergence run
# expects to find already there.
BOX_DESCRIPTION="Server-class Debian 13, creds-free — box mints it, the posture and the join stay yours"
BOX_IMAGE="images:debian/13/cloud"
BOX_USER="ops"
BOX_CPU="4"
BOX_MEMORY="8GiB"
BOX_DISK="60GiB"
BOX_REQUIRE_VM="1"
BOX_AUTOSTART="1"
